      {
        "kind": "text",
        "heading": "Antiderivatives &amp; the indefinite integral",
        "body": {
          "en": "Reversing differentiation, \\( F \\) is an antiderivative of \\( f \\) if \\( F'=f \\). Since constants vanish under differentiation, antiderivatives carry a \\( +C \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power (n ≠ −1)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int x^{n}\\,dx=\\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Reciprocal",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,dx=\\ln|x|+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponential",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int e^{x}\\,dx=e^{x}+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sine",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int \\sin x\\,dx=-\\cos x+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cosine",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int \\cos x\\,dx=\\sin x+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Linearity",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int (af+bg)=a\\!\\int\\! f+b\\!\\int\\! g \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area under \\( f(x)=x^2 \\) from \\( 0 \\) to \\( 2 \\).</p><p>An antiderivative is \\( F(x)=\\tfrac{x^3}{3} \\). Evaluating (using the Fundamental Theorem, next chapter):</p>\\[ \\int_0^2 x^2\\,dx=\\Big[\\tfrac{x^3}{3}\\Big]_0^2=\\tfrac{8}{3}-0=\\tfrac{8}{3}\\approx 2.667. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
